<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Royal Niger Company</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Royal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger</a> Company was a British chartered company that held a commercial monopoly and administrative powers over territories along the lower Niger in the 1880s and 1890s. Its charter was revoked in 1900, when its territories passed to the British government and became part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorates</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto Caliphate</a> profile identifies the company's monopoly as the start of the British threat that ended in the conquest of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphate</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/royal-niger-company.jpg" alt="Royal Niger Company" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bohr · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Royal_Niger_Company_flag.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
